# Request a return

- Customers can request a return only for an order marked delivered with a recorded delivery time. {#require-delivery}
  e.g. An order is still paid -> requesting a return fails with "Only delivered orders can be returned".

- Customers can submit a return exactly 30 days after delivery, but receive a rejection once more than 30 days have elapsed. {#enforce-return-window}
  e.g. An order was delivered at 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z -> a return at 2026-01-31T00:00:00Z is accepted, while one a millisecond later is rejected.

- Customers must include at least one item in a return request. {#require-items}
  e.g. A delivered order is within the return window, but the request has no items -> it fails with "A return needs at least one item".

- Customers receive a rejection for a return entry whose product is absent from the order. {#require-ordered-product}
  e.g. An order contains only wool socks, and the customer requests a headlamp return -> the request fails because the headlamp is not on the order.

- Customers must specify a whole-number quantity of at least one for each return entry. {#require-positive-whole-quantity}
  e.g. A customer requests a return of 1.5 wool socks -> the request fails with "Quantity must be a whole number of at least 1".

